  🧠 The[0m[2m simulation[0m[2m confirms[0m[2m both issues[0m[2m perfectly[0m[2m:
     
     1[0m[2m. **[0m[2mDuplicate processing[0m[2m**: Every[0m[2m job is[0m[2m picked up[0m[2m by all[0m[2m 5[0m[2m workers.[0m[2m You[0m[2m can[0m[2m see `[[0m[2mWorker[0m[2m 0][0m[2m picked up[0m[2m job[0m[2m 1`[0m[2m through `[[0m[2mWorker[0m[2m 4][0m[2m picked up[0m[2m job[0m[2m 1`[0m[2m for[0m[2m every single[0m[2m job.[0m[2m This is[0m[2m because `[0m[2mdequeue[0m[2m()`[0m[2m checks[0m[2m if[0m[2m status[0m[2m is "[0m[2mpending",[0m[2m then `[0m[2mawait asyncio[0m[2m.sleep([0m[2m0.[0m[2m01)`[0m[2m yields control[0m[2m, allowing[0m[2m other workers[0m[2m to also[0m[2m see the[0m[2m job as[0m[2m pending[0m[2m and pick[0m[2m it up[0m[2m,[0m[2m before finally[0m[2m setting status[0m[2m to "[0m[2mprocessing".[0m[2m
     
     2.[0m[2m **Van[0m[2mishing failures[0m[2m**: The[0m[2m bad[0m[2m jobs ([0m[2m11[0m[2m and[0m[2m 12)[0m[2m are picked[0m[2m up by[0m[2m all workers[0m[2m, fail[0m[2m in[0m[2m all workers[0m[2m, but[0m[2m end[0m[2m up with[0m[2m status[0m[2m "processing[0m[2m" ([0m[2mstuck[0m[2m:[0m[2m 2)[0m[2m instead of[0m[2m "failed[0m[2m". This[0m[2m is because[0m[2m `worker[0m[2m.py`[0m[2m catches exceptions[0m[2m but never[0m[2m calls `[0m[2mqueue.fail[0m[2m()`.[0m[2m The `[0m[2mfail()`[0m[2m method in[0m[2m `job[0m[2m_queue.py[0m[2m` has[0m[2m retry[0m[2m logic that[0m[2m would eventually[0m[2m mark them[0m[2m as failed[0m[2m after max[0m[2m_retries,[0m[2m but since[0m[2m `[0m[2mworker.py[0m[2m` never[0m[2m calls it[0m[2m, the[0m[2m jobs just[0m[2m stay in[0m[2m "processing[0m[2m" forever[0m[2m.
     
     Now[0m[2m let me[0m[2m fix both[0m[2m issues:[0m[2m
     
     **Fix[0m[2m 1[0m[2m -[0m[2m Duplicate[0m[2m processing (`[0m[2mjob_queue[0m[2m.py:[0m[2mdequeue[0m[2m`)**[0m[2m:
     Move[0m[2m the status[0m[2m change to[0m[2m "processing[0m[2m" BEFORE[0m[2m the[0m[2m `await[0m[2m asyncio.sleep[0m[2m(0[0m[2m.01[0m[2m)`. Actually[0m[2m, the[0m[2m sleep is[0m[2m there[0m[2m to simulate[0m[2m I[0m[2m/O,[0m[2m but the[0m[2m critical[0m[2m thing[0m[2m is that[0m[2m the state[0m[2m transition happens[0m[2m before yielding[0m[2m control.[0m[2m
     
     ```[0m[2mpython[0m[2m
     async def[0m[2m dequeue(self[0m[2m) ->[0m[2m Optional[[0m[2mDict]:[0m[2m
         for[0m[2m job in[0m[2m self._[0m[2mjobs.values[0m[2m():[0m[2m
             if job[0m[2m["status[0m[2m"] ==[0m[2m "pending[0m[2m":[0m[2m
                 job["[0m[2mstatus"][0m[2m = "[0m[2mprocessing"[0m[2m
                 await[0m[2m asyncio.sleep[0m[2m(0[0m[2m.01[0m[2m)[0m[2m
                 return job[0m[2m
